<p class="p2">Summary:</p>
<p class="p2">1. Primary Request and Intent:</p>
<p class="p2"><span class="Apple-converted-space">   </span>The user requested to migrate the Honda Canada homepage (https://www.honda.ca/en/) to AEM Edge Delivery Services (EDS). This involves using the excat page migration workflow to analyze, structure, and convert the source page content into an</p>
<p class="p2">EDS-compatible format with proper block structure for the Universal Editor (xwalk).</p>
<p class="p1"><br></p>
<p class="p2">2. Key Technical Concepts:</p>
<p class="p2"><span class="Apple-converted-space">   </span>- **AEM Edge Delivery Services (EDS)**: Adobe's content delivery platform</p>
<p class="p2"><span class="Apple-converted-space">   </span>- **Xwalk/Crosswalk**: Universal Editor-based authoring (identified by AEM author instance in fstab.yaml)</p>
<p class="p2"><span class="Apple-converted-space">   </span>- **Block Variants**: Custom block implementations based on vanilla blocks (e.g., carousel-hero, hero-video)</p>
<p class="p2"><span class="Apple-converted-space">   </span>- **Block Collection**: Library of reusable EDS blocks from `https://github.com/adobe-rnd/aem-block-collection-xwalk`</p>
<p class="p2"><span class="Apple-converted-space">   </span>- **MCP Tools**: start_xwalk_workflow, advance_workflow, get_vanilla_block_code, get_all_blocks_catalog</p>
<p class="p2"><span class="Apple-converted-space">   </span>- **Block Table Markdown**: AEM-specific markdown format using `+---+` table syntax for blocks</p>
<p class="p2"><span class="Apple-converted-space">   </span>- **David's Model**: Prioritize authoring experience, minimize blocks, prefer default content</p>
