<p class="p1"><br></p>
<p class="p2">⏺ Created tools/importer/import.js. The file includes: <span class="Apple-converted-space">                                                                                                                                                              </span>09:38 PM<span class="Apple-converted-space">  </span>claude-opus-4-5-20251101</p>
<p class="p1"><br></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="Apple-converted-space">  </span>Features:</p>
<p class="p2"><span class="Apple-converted-space">  </span>- Block Parser Registry - Maps all 4 block parsers (carousel-hero, hero-video, cards-promo, columns-banner)</p>
<p class="p2"><span class="Apple-converted-space">  </span>- Template Detection - Uses page-templates.json to match URLs to templates</p>
<p class="p2"><span class="Apple-converted-space">  </span>- transformDOM() - Main transformation function that:</p>
<p class="p2"><span class="Apple-converted-space">    </span>- Detects the template for the URL</p>
<p class="p2"><span class="Apple-converted-space">    </span>- Finds and parses blocks using registered parsers</p>
<p class="p2"><span class="Apple-converted-space">    </span>- Replaces source elements with AEM block tables</p>
<p class="p2"><span class="Apple-converted-space">    </span>- Cleans up scripts, styles, and empty elements</p>
<p class="p2"><span class="Apple-converted-space">    </span>- Extracts and appends page metadata</p>
<p class="p2"><span class="Apple-converted-space">  </span>- generateDocumentPath() - Generates the document path from URL</p>
<p class="p2"><span class="Apple-converted-space">  </span>- createBlockTable() - Helper to create AEM-formatted block tables</p>
<p class="p2"><span class="Apple-converted-space">  </span>- extractMetadata() - Extracts title and meta tags</p>
<p class="p1"><br></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="Apple-converted-space">  </span>Exports:</p>
<p class="p2"><span class="Apple-converted-space">  </span>export { transformDOM, generateDocumentPath }</p>
<p class="p2"><span class="Apple-converted-space">  </span>export default { transformDOM, generateDocumentPath, blockParsers, pageTemplates }</p>
<p class="p1"><br></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="Apple-converted-space">  </span>The import script is now ready for use with the helix-importer-ui for bulk page imports. You can use it to import additional Honda Canada pages that follow the same template structure.</p>
<p class="p1"><br></p>
<p class="p2">∴ Thinking…</p>
<p class="p1"><br></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="Apple-converted-space">  </span>I've created the import.js file and updated the todo list. The user may want to preview the migration now. Should I offer to start the local dev server or do anything else?</p>
